  "description": "ZEVFIT crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n n c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H136 Eu9 O42 S8 1-,C2 H8 N1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 10 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1C (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1D (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1E (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1F (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1G (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.638-5.145 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.81-173.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [(CH3)2NH2][Eu9(TC4A)2(μ3-O)8(μ4-O)2(H2O)24]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 24 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
